## Topic: Dense Embeddings and Semantic Similarity

### Problem Statement

Traditional TF-IDF vectors rely on exact word matching and often fail when two sentences have the same meaning but use different vocabulary.

Dense embeddings solve this problem by representing text as numerical vectors in a high-dimensional space, allowing machines to understand semantic meaning rather than simple keyword overlap. Similar meanings produce similar vectors.

